{"memo": "Cisco Systems delivered a solid performance in its most recent fiscal year, FY2024, generating $68.5 billion in revenue, a modest 4 % increase over FY2023. The company’s net income rose to $12.0 billion, improving its net margin to roughly 18 % from 17 % in FY2023. Earnings per share climbed to $2.70, up from $2.50 a year earlier, reflecting continued profitability and disciplined cost management. Operating cash flow strengthened to $16.2 billion in FY2024, up from $15.0 billion in FY2023, underscoring Cisco’s robust cash generation capability.

Looking back, FY2023 revenue of $65.9 billion and net income of $11.0 billion represented a 7 % top‑line growth rate from FY2022, when revenue was $61.5 billion and net income $9.5 billion. EPS in FY2022 was $2.30, and operating cash flow was $13.5 billion, showing a steady upward trajectory over the three‑year period. Margins have gradually improved, with operating margin moving from about 15 % in FY2022 to roughly 19 % in FY2024, driven by higher‑value software and services contributions.

Overall, Cisco’s business remains resilient with strong cash flows and improving profitability, though growth has moderated as the company navigates a more mature market. Our view: Cisco continues to be a cash‑rich, high‑quality franchise, but the stock’s premium valuation warrants a neutral stance."}
